## Recommended Pattern: `PersistentComponentState` + Scoped Service + `CascadingValue` in a Root Interactive Component

Given per-page interactivity with a **static** layout, the core challenge is that static-rendered components (like your header) can't re-render from server-side state changes alone. Here's the proven approach:

---

### 1. Make the Layout Interactive

The simplest fix: wrap the relevant layout section in an **interactive boundary**:

```razor
@* MainLayout.razor — remains static *@
<HeadContent>...</HeadContent>

<div class="page">
    <ThemeRoot>           @* ← this becomes the interactive shell *@
        <Sidebar />
        <main>@Body</main>
    </ThemeRoot>
</div>
```

```razor
@* ThemeRoot.razor *@
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<CascadingValue Value="themeState" IsFixed="false">
    @ChildContent
</CascadingValue>

@code {
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; } = default!;
    private ThemeState themeState = default!;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        themeState = ThemeService; // injected scoped service
        ThemeService.OnChange += StateHasChanged;
    }
}
```

### 2. Scoped `ThemeService` (per-circuit isolation)

```csharp
// Registered as: builder.Services.AddScoped<ThemeService>();
public class ThemeService
{
    public Theme CurrentTheme { get; private set; } = Theme.System;
    public string AccentColor { get; private set; } = "#0078d4";

    public event Action? OnChange;

    public void SetTheme(Theme theme) { CurrentTheme = theme; OnChange?.Invoke(); }
    public void SetAccent(string color) { AccentColor = color; OnChange?.Invoke(); }
}

public enum Theme { Light, Dark, System }
```

### 3. Any component consumes it

```razor
@inject ThemeService ThemeService
@implements IDisposable

<button @onclick="Toggle">Current: @ThemeService.CurrentTheme</button>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() => ThemeService.OnChange += StateHasChanged;
    public void Dispose() => ThemeService.OnChange -= StateHasChanged;
    void Toggle() => ThemeService.SetTheme(
        ThemeService.CurrentTheme == Theme.Light ? Theme.Dark : Theme.Light);
}
```

---

### Why This Works

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| App-wide read/write | Scoped DI service injected anywhere |
| Immediate cross-component updates | `OnChange` event triggers re-render in all subscribers |
| Static layout area updates | `ThemeRoot` makes the layout shell interactive — it re-renders children on change |
| Per-user isolation | `AddScoped` = one instance per circuit |
| Persists across enhanced nav | Circuit stays alive during enhanced navigation; scoped service persists |

---

### Key Insight

With per-page interactivity, your **layout is static by default and won't re-render**. The fix is to introduce a single interactive component (`ThemeRoot`) high in the tree that owns the cascading state. Since enhanced navigation preserves the circuit, the scoped service survives page transitions naturally.

